<title>UK: UK's Halifax conversion to cost 413 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK's Halifax conversion to cost 413 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's largest home loans maker, the Halifax Building Society, said in a statement on Thursday that the cost of its coversion into a bank and provisions against its acquisition of the Leeds Permanent Building Society would be 413 million stg.</p>
<p>The Halifax said in a statement with nine month earnings on Thursday that it was taking a charge of 208.9 million for merger and integration costs plus  51.5 million on the disposal of fixed assets. British newspapers quoted a Halifax spokesman as saying that the cost of lawyers, bankers and advisors will be 153 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 7717</p>
